{"assignees":[{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa","databaseId":12109493}],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"### Background\n\nThe Projects page calls `gh api user` on every start to resolve `assignee:@me` in view filters. The login is already stored locally by `gh auth login` (hosts.yml) and can be read with `gh config get -h <host> user`: no API request, and it follows `gh auth switch`.\n\n### Proposal\n\n- Resolution order: the config node `github-login \"alice\"` → `gh config get -h <host> user` (the host comes from the remote detection in `remote.rs`) → unknown.\n- Move the lookup into `src/core/` and share it between the GitHub and Projects pages (resolved once per session).\n- Keep `gh api user` only as a last resort for setups where `gh config get` yields nothing (e.g. token auth without a `user` entry in hosts.yml). Save that result to `~/.cache/vig/viewer.json` so later starts do not call the API again.\n- Fixtures: add `config_get_-h_github.com_user.out`; keep `api_user_--jq_.login.out` for the fallback.\n\n### Scope\n\n- `src/core/` — new module for the viewer login\n- `src/core/config/` — `github-login`, validation and tests\n- `src/projects/{state,domain/client}.rs` — use the shared lookup instead of `gh api user`\n- `src/fixtures.rs` — record `gh config get`\n- Config Reference (en / ja)\n\n### Notes\n\nRead-only as before; the login is only used to match assignees / reviewers locally.","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-11-04T04:21:15Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":208,"state":"OPEN","title":"Resolve the signed-in login without an API call (gh config get, github-login)"}
